I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the git add … || true step does nothing, as the harness intends. I first committed it by mistake with git add -f. I reverted that local, unpushed commit, so HEAD is back at ecc5fa14 and the file is still on disk.

Main finding: #1029 is reproduced, and I found where it comes from. @yuanhao filed it with a public screenshot showing yoyo printing raw ## and **. I ran a temporary test against MarkdownRenderer and restored the file afterwards; src/ is clean.
• **Headings:** the `#` markers always print, whether the line arrives whole or in pieces. The heading branch in `render_line` (`markdown.rs:660`) wraps the raw line in bold and cyan, never removes the #, and never formats bold or italic inside the heading.
• **Lists:** bold that is split across chunks right after a list or numbered-list marker leaks, e.g. `["- **","apply**: x\n"]` prints `• **apply**: x`. Cause: `try_resolve_block_prefix (~line 420–450) renders the rest of the line with render_inline instead of the #661 version that holds an unmatched **` until its partner arrives. The same text arriving as one whole line renders cleanly.
• **Minor:** a quote line (>) split across chunks gets an extra space and its italic styling is never switched off.
• **Existing tests pin the bug:** test_md_header_rendering and test_md_header_h2 assert the heading with its hashes. The fix has to change them deliberately, not delete them.
• **Precedent:** Codex made the same fix. Its normal display drops the `#`, a raw mode keeps it, and its tests check that streamed output matches whole-text output. The planner still has to decide what a heading looks like with colour off, because removing the # there would leave nothing marking it as a heading.

Other notes for the planner:
• **#1030:** a typo in `cost_warn_usd` turns the spending budget off silently, whether it comes from the config file, the flag or the env var. It's a small fix outside dispatch, and the trajectory says to avoid dispatch because it took 4 of the last 8 self-driven changes.
• **Size limit:** `commands_risk_unhittable.rs` is 36 lines over the 2000-line cap and isn't listed as an exception. 14 more lines would make `cargo test` fail and revert the whole task.
• Health: the binary answers PONG, and yoyo grep on a missing directory exits 2. The last 10 sessions completed 2/2 tasks each with no reverts, and CI is green. The 00:09 evolve run shows as cancelled; I believe it's a duplicate of this session's run, but didn't check.

